    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1326">

                <pb facs="1079" n="1069" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1069"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.7146/3–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-11T18:00:00-05:00">March 11, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. Urtel 368 March 8. Dept concurs recommendation last paragraph reftel but
                    since circumstances may arise making desirable transmission occasional coded
                    message urgent nature behalf your consular colleagues Dept prefers not instruct
                    but leave matter your discretion.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d1326-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1326-f1" n="43" xml:id="d1326-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 839, May 16, noon, the Consul General informed the Department
                    that he had informed the British Consulate that British code messages would be
                    accepted in case of emergency (125.7146/5–1649).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
